      <journal id="j-fg-ground" title="God as living foundation" kicker="Why Gate Bedrock" unlockAfter="fg-ground" scoreFromHeldTier="true">
        <p>Order, reason, and ought are not free-floating. Finite nature cannot hold them up. Cosmo isn’t the ground, and Ansel isn’t either. The foundation is the living God — not a dead first brick.</p>
        <p>Acts 17:24–28 names the God who made the world and gives life and breath: in him we live and move and have our being. Augustine’s restless heart and Aquinas’s ipsum esse read that same living source. This beat is distinct from the later first-mover and kalām walks. It is the case-for-God foundation under the trusts you already spend.</p>
        <sources>
          <source>Acts 17:24–28</source>
          <source>Augustine, Confessions I.1</source>
          <source>Aquinas, ST I, q.3; q.44</source>
        </sources>
      </journal>
